{# Alertmanager's own UI, where the operator lists alerts and inhibitions and manages silences
   (M6 B-6b, #6690). The design is answer 1 (b) of
   docs/target-architecture/monitoring/alertmanager-ui-and-readers.md.

   The UI can silence every page, so the `authelia` chain is the control, and the rule it
   meets is the hand-written `two_factor` rule for `group:admins` with the `deny` after it
   (roles/k8s/authelia/templates/config-secret.yaml.j2, M6 B-6a). Without that rule the
   `*.local` wildcard would pass this host at one_factor.

   LAN-ONLY, and it ignores k8s_public_route, in the shape of prometheus-ingressroute.yaml.j2.
   The client set is the read door's: the LAN plus the node addresses a host process arrives
   as, so the `claude-ui` browser on either node reaches it. Pods and WireGuard peers are
   excluded.

   The GET-only read door (alertmanager-read-ingressroute.yaml.j2) shares this host. Traefik
   ranks routers by rule length when none sets `priority`, and the door's rule is the longer,
   so a GET on /api/v2/alerts or /api/v2/silences reaches it without Authelia, and every other
   request lands here. ansible/tests/k8s/test_alertmanager_read_route.py is the guard. #}
{% set clients = [lan_subnet] + k3s_cni0_gateways + k3s_flannel_node_ips %}
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: IngressRoute
metadata:
  name: alertmanager
  namespace: {{ k8s_observability_namespace }}
spec:
  entryPoints:
    - https
  routes:
    - kind: Rule
      # OR'd ClientIP matchers, NOT ClientIP(a, b): the multi-arg form fails rule parsing on
      # this Traefik and the router vanishes (prometheus-ingressroute.yaml.j2).
      match: "Host(`alertmanager.local.{{ domain }}`) && ({% for cidr in clients %}ClientIP(`{{ cidr }}`){% if not loop.last %} || {% endif %}{% endfor %})"
      middlewares:
        - name: rate-limit
        - name: authelia
      services:
        - name: alertmanager
          port: 9093
  tls:
{% if k8s_tls_cert_resolver %}
    certResolver: {{ k8s_tls_cert_resolver }}
{% endif %}
    options:
      name: modern
{% if k8s_tls_cert_resolver %}
    domains:
      - main: "{{ domain }}"
        sans:
          - "*.{{ domain }}"
          - "*.local.{{ domain }}"
{% endif %}
